    {
      "id": "9c0b60ff7e4c58b813751434d90beb7420faf401",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 812778574,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Two comments from a quick review, let me know if I missed anything:\n\n1. ws_return.h needs to return an invalid placeholder, that's the whole point to use it, to signal a programming error without crashing, so if you really wanted to return the empty string for a null input, that should be done in bytes_to_str_punct_maxlen() instead, by replacing the call to ws_return_str_if_null().\n\n2. Does it really fix anything to return `\"\"` instead of `\"(null)\"`? Seems to me like it's just hiding the problem. That produces an empty `Octets:` display. Is that desirable? If the dissector expects octets and there are none, surely the fix is not to display octets-colon-nothing, right? Maybe there is a bug with the tvb offset, or maybe there should be an expert info instead, or maybe even the display should be `\"Octets field is empty\"`.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-01-17T15:46:24.327Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-01-17T16:16:35.400Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 135530573,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2022-01-18T13:17:48.959Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 5922,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 812814098,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "1. The sole function that calls `ws_return_str_if_null` (a macro) is actually `bytes_to_str_punct_maxlen`. If you prefer I can make the check in bytes_to_str_punct_maxlen, but that would mean to totally remove ws_return_str_if_null accordingly.\n\n1. A new tree is created under `Element` that reads `Octet String: <MISSING>`. Isn't that enough? Before the patch we had `Element, Octets: (null pointer)/Octet String: <MISSING>`",
          "author": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-01-17T16:16:35.342Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-01-17T16:16:35.342Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 135530573,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2022-01-18T13:17:48.959Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 5922,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 812867271,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "1. I think you should fix the dissectors instead with a null check or something else, but in any case please don't change the ws_return.h header. You can remove ws_return_str_if_null() from bytes_to_str_punct_maxlen, if you think this function should accept a NULL value (I don't, why would you try to convert to a byte string a NULL array?).\n\n2. OK, if you think it's enough, go ahead. I don't have time to properly follow-up on this issue.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
