    {
      "id": "da3a8e837d2aab7f4e9dc8610f1cef6cd124882d",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 813009405,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Perhaps `ws_return_str_if_null()` and `ws_return_str_if_zero()` should support an exception mechanism, calling a registered handler to report the error, with the default handler reporting the error with `ws_critical()`, and with the dissection process registering a handler that uses `REPORT_DISSECTOR_BUG()` in the top-level `TRY` and unregistering it when dissection is done?\n\nThat way, the dissector bug will show up in the dissection, so it pokes the user in the eye and hopefully gets them to report the bug.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-01-17T20:58:48.171Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-01-17T20:58:48.171Z",
